Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 14:04:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] fix remaining GLM audit bugs (3/5/6); pextrw
 oracle-verified vs 4 compilers

pextrw godbolt-oracle verification: the memory-destination fix from the
previous commit is now byte-identical to FOUR reference toolchains via
the Compiler Explorer API (binaryObject disassembly): gcc trunk, clang
trunk, icx 2026.0.0, icc 2021.10 all emit 66 0F 3A 15 (SSE4.1) for mem
destinations and 66 0F C5 (legacy) for reg destinations - exactly what
lccc now produces. New asm-diff casefile sse_extract_insert.s locks in
pextrw/pextrb/pextrd/pextrq/pinsrw byte parity with GNU as (reg, mem,
REX-extended forms).

BUG-3 (i686 float->i128): emit_float_to_i128_call_impl loaded F64
sources with flds (4 of 8 bytes -> garbage). F64 now travels as a
64-bit pair and loads with fldl; F32 keeps the flds path. Frontend
rejects __int128 on i686, so this was latent, but the IR path is now
correct for internal users.

BUG-5 (AArch64 NEON): ld1/st1/ld2/../st4 (both element and
multi-register forms) and tbl/tbx now validate that register lists are
consecutive modulo 32. Only Rt is encoded - hardware derives the rest,
so {v0,v2} silently accessed the WRONG registers before. Verified:
consecutive lists assemble, {v0.16b, v2.16b} is rejected with a clear
diagnostic (matching GNU as).

BUG-6 (F128 i128-cast): the trait default panicked via unimplemented!()
on non-x86. aarch64 now calls __floattitf/__floatuntitf and stores the
q0 result (16 bytes) via a real emit_store_f128_xmm0 override; the
trait default falls back to the acc-pair store (correct for RISC-V
LP64 where the result travels in a0/a1) instead of panicking.

641 lib tests, 153 regressions, 50 correctness, full asm-diff suite:
all green.
