From b163f4a95907cbc8d5501ff28f808fb99ded8314 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 14:21:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] x86 assembler: fix symbol+expr-chain data parsing and
 8-byte symdiff truncation

Both bugs came from the current_tasks backlog (kernel standalone-link
errors) and were verified against GNU as before fixing:

1. `.quad symbol + (expr) - const + const` (the kernel's
   level1_fixmap_pgt + (N << 12) pattern): parse_data_values split at
   the first " - " and treated everything left of it - including
   arithmetic - as a SYMBOL NAME, emitting a relocation against the
   nonexistent "level1_fixmap_pgt + (2 << 12)". A new
   parse_symbol_expr_chain folds the whole constant tail first:
   R_X86_64_64 base_sym+0x2008, byte-identical to GNU as.

2. `.quad a - b` with a < b: resolve_internal_relocations' patch loop
   had no 8-byte case - the catch-all wrote 4 bytes (i32), leaving the
   sign-extension upper half zero (f8 ff ff ff 00 00 00 00 instead of
   f8 ff ff ff ff ff ff ff). Same-section .quad differences of >4GiB
   magnitude would also have truncated. Full 64-bit patch added.

New asm-diff casefile data_expressions.s locks in both patterns plus
symdiff-with-addend chains; .data payloads and relocation tables are
byte-identical to GNU as. 641 lib tests, 153 regressions, 50
correctness, 86 linker tests: all green.
